  "note": "王府前院、王府校场 (native:guanbei/palace_yard, drill; 关北 B): the forecourt behind the faded red gate — the whitewashed screen wall scored with old knife marks, the yard swept bare (the one clean place in town), two flag poles with the 王府's banners, the lanterns under the hall's eave, three steps up to its door; the drill yard east of it — the posts with their left shoulders hacked away, the butts, the hitching rail with two ponies, chips and sand, 郭承 and his men. Old and plain: rammed-earth walls, faded red woodwork, the 石青 scrollwork on the beams.",
